e><name><surname>Behari</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gralla</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahlbusch</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nimsky</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neuronavigation: concept, techniques and applications</article-title><source>Neurol India</source><year>2002</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>244</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12391447</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR23"><label>23.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Grunert, P., Darabi, K., Espinosa, J. &#x00026; Filippi, R. Computer-aided navigation in neurosurgery. <italic>Neurosurg Rev</italic><bold>26</bold>, 73&#x02013;99 discussion 100-101 (2003).</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR24"><label>24.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Neuronavigation-guided focused ultrasound-induced blood-brain barrier opening: a preliminary study in swine</article-title><source>AJNR Am J Neuroradiol</source><year>2013</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>120</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3174/ajnr.A3150</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">22723060</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CR25"><label>25.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Treeby</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><name><surname>Jaros</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rendell</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>BT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modeling nonlinear ultrasound propagation in heterogeneous media with power law absorption using a k-space pseudospectral method</article-title><source>J Acoust Soc Am</source><year>2012<